<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3795" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">artĕmon</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">artĕmo</span></b> , Lucil. ap. <i><span class="en">Charis.
			p. 99</span></i> P.), ōnis, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτέμων</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A sail put upon the mast above the main-sail</i>,
				<i>a top-sail</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 50,
				16, 242</span></i>; * <i><span class="en">Vulg. Act.
				27, 40</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The guiding-pulley of a machine for raising
			weights</i>, * <i><span class="en">Vitr. 10, 5</span></i>.</div>
